    {"id": 9, "type": "manual", "slot": "(b) locus argument",
     "desc": "Part (b): the argument must use the defining property, not the equation. From the point at 2 and 4 the distance to the focus at 2 and 0 is 4, and the distance to the vertical directrix at x equal to -2 is 2 minus -2, which is also 4. Equal distances is exactly what puts a point on the parabola. Award no credit for substituting into y squared equals 8x, which checks the algebra rather than the locus definition the question asks about.",
