    {"id": 10, "type": "manual", "slot": "(b) describe the locus",
     "desc": "Part (b): the simplified equation is a circle centred at the origin with radius 4, and a complete answer says all three things, shape, centre and size, and points to the equation as the reason. The surprise worth naming is that the two fixed points have vanished from the answer entirely: the sum-of-squared-distances condition does not depend on which of them a point is nearer. An answer giving only the shape, with no centre or radius, is half credit.",
